Q: how to make UITextView height dynamic according to text length? A: <p><strong>Swift 4+</strong></p>
<p>This can be done with <strong>autolayout</strong>! I'll explain the most simple use case. Let's say there is only a <code>UITextView</code> in your <code>UITableViewCell</code>.</p>
<ul>
<li>Fit the <code>textView</code> to the <code>contentView</code> with constraints.</li>
<li>Disable scrolling for the <code>textView</code>.</li>
<li>Update the <code>tableView</code> on <code>textViewDidChange</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p>That's all!</p>
<pre><code>protocol TextViewUpdateProtocol {
    func textViewChanged()
}

class TextViewCell: UITableViewCell {

    //MARK: Reuse ID
    static let identifier = debugDescription()

    //MARK: UI Element(s)
    /// Reference of the parent table view so that it can be updated
    var textViewUpdateDelegate: TextViewUpdateProtocol!

    lazy var textView: UITextView = {
        let textView = UITextView()
        textView.isScrollEnabled = false
        textView.delegate = self
        textView.layer.borderColor = UIColor.lightGray.cgColor
        textView.layer.borderWidth = 1
        textView.translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = false
        return textView
    }()

    //MARK: Padding Variable(s)
    let padding: CGFloat = 50

    //MARK: Initializer(s)
    override init(style: UITableViewCell.CellStyle, reuseIdentifier: String?) {
        super.init(style: style, reuseIdentifier: reuseIdentifier)

        addSubviews()
        addConstraints()

        textView.becomeFirstResponder()
    }

    //MARK: Helper Method(s)
    func addSubviews() {
        contentView.addSubview(textView)
    }

    func addConstraints() {
        textView.leadingAnchor  .constraint(equalTo: contentView.leadingAnchor, constant: padding).isActive = true
        textView.trailingAnchor .constraint(equalTo: contentView.trailingAnchor, constant: -padding).isActive = true
        textView.topAnchor      .constraint(equalTo: contentView.topAnchor, constant: padding).isActive = true
        textView.bottomAnchor   .constraint(equalTo: contentView.bottomAnchor, constant: -padding).isActive = true
    }

    required init?(coder aDecoder: NSCoder) {
        fatalError(&quot;init(coder:) has not been implemented&quot;)
    }

}

extension TextViewCell: UITextViewDelegate {

    func textViewDidChange(_ textView: UITextView) {
        textViewUpdateDelegate.textViewChanged()
    }

}
</code></pre>
<p>Now you have to inherit implement the protocol in your <code>ViewController</code>.</p>
<pre><code>extension ViewController: TextViewUpdateProtocol {

    func textViewChanged() {
        tableView.beginUpdates()
        tableView.endUpdates()
    }

}
</code></pre>
<p>Check out my <a href="https://github.com/rakeshashastri/resizing-textView-in-tableviewcell" rel="nofollow noreferrer">repo</a> for the full implementation.</p>

Q: MongoDB.Bson.BsonSerializationException after C# driver update to 3.5.0 A: <p>After some research and trial and error, you are getting the mentioned error as the bug fix was introducted in <a href="https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/CSHARP-4040" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Serialization ignores discriminator field when checking for duplicate field names</a>.</p>
<p>From the <em>BsonClassMap.cs</em> code change in this PR: <a href="https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-csharp-driver/pull/1684/files#diff-d3dfbcf83190135d81d0365e98a792e25a39b0001de6154937aa4af42462dd3dR1329-R1342" rel="nofollow noreferrer">CSHARP-4040: Fix bug when using field with same element name as discriminator #1684</a>,</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>if (discriminatorConvention != null)
{
    var conflictingMemberMap = _allMemberMaps.FirstOrDefault(memberMap =&gt; memberMap.ElementName == discriminatorConvention.ElementName);

    if (conflictingMemberMap != null)
    {
        var fieldOrProperty = conflictingMemberMap.MemberInfo is FieldInfo ? &quot;field&quot; : &quot;property&quot;;

        throw new BsonSerializationException(
            $&quot;The discriminator element name cannot be {discriminatorConvention.ElementName} &quot; +
            $&quot;because it is already being used by the {fieldOrProperty} {conflictingMemberMap.MemberName} of type {_classType.FullName}&quot;);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>This will restrict that the discriminator field name in <code>ElementName</code> cannot be the same as the property, field, or <code>[BsonElement]</code> name in the class.</p>
<p>From my understanding, this change will enforce that you should use <code>_t</code> as discriminator field (which is not possible to you that you need to migrate the data) or you cannot have the same property name as your discriminator field name in your class.</p>
<p>In one of my testing scenario, found out that this issue is no longer happen when you add the <code>[BsonIgnore]</code> attribute to <code>SecurityType</code> property. This will result the <code>SecurityType</code> will not be (de)serialized for twice.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>[BsonIgnore]
public Security SecurityType { get; init; }
</code></pre>
<p>However, as I know with <code>[BsonIgnore]</code> could result the property will be excluded in the insert/update operation, this property will be excluded. Hence, <strong>this approach is not suggested</strong> and just for your information (you may try this behavior).</p>
<hr />
<p>At this moment, I would suggest you not to upgrade to version 3.5 and <a href="https://jira.mongodb.org/secure/CreateIssue!default.jspa" rel="nofollow noreferrer">raise an issue in MongoDB Jira board</a> on working the discriminator as a property in the class. If upgrade to version 3.5 is a must and there is no solution from MongoDB team, you should look for <em>disable</em> the <code>SecurityTypeDiscriminatorConvention</code> and create the class instance based on <code>SecurityType</code> manually.</p>
<hr />
<p>According to the <a href="https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/CSHARP-5752?focusedCommentId=8116940&amp;focusedId=8116940&amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-8116940" rel="nofollow noreferrer">comment</a> in the <a href="https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/CSHARP-5752" rel="nofollow noreferrer">reported issue</a>, a temporary solution was introduced from the <strong>version 3.5.2</strong> by adding the below line:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>AppContext.SetSwitch(&quot;Switch.MongoDB.Driver.DisableDiscriminatorFieldConflictCheck&quot;, true); 
</code></pre>
<p>this will prevent the member map conflict checkng for the discriminator field in the <a href="https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-csharp-driver/blob/b139e1060a5c2186955b0420e48eaaacce6f8168/src/MongoDB.Bson/Serialization/BsonClassMap.cs#L1340-L1342" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>EnsureNoMemberMapConflicts</code></a> method.</p>
